## Vercel Speed Insights Implementation

Successfully implemented Vercel Speed Insights for the Next.js application as requested.

### Changes Made

1. **Installed Package**
   - Added `@vercel/speed-insights` (v1.3.1) to project dependencies
   - Used npm (matching the project's existing package manager)

2. **Modified Files**
   - `src/app/layout.tsx`: Added SpeedInsights component to root layout
     - Imported `SpeedInsights` from `@vercel/speed-insights/next`
     - Added `<SpeedInsights />` component inside the `<body>` tag after the `{children}` wrapper
     - Placed after the I18nProvider to ensure it doesn't interfere with the main content

3. **Updated Dependencies**
   - `package.json`: Added @vercel/speed-insights dependency
   - `package-lock.json`: Updated with new package and its dependencies

### Implementation Details

This project uses Next.js 16.1.1 with App Router, so the implementation followed the Next.js 13.5+ approach:
- Used the `/next` import path for automatic App Router integration
- Added the component directly to the root layout without needing a client component wrapper
- The component will automatically collect and report Core Web Vitals to Vercel

### Verification

✓ TypeScript compilation passes with no errors
✓ No linting errors introduced in modified files
✓ All changes follow existing code patterns and conventions
✓ Lock file properly updated with new dependencies

### Notes

- The SpeedInsights component will automatically track Core Web Vitals (LCP, FID, CLS, etc.)
- Data will be visible in the Vercel dashboard once the application is deployed
- No additional configuration is required for basic functionality
- The component is lightweight and won't impact application performance
